! REPRODUCER, a MODEL finding (docs/NEXT.md, "G2.1 CHAPTER 4: LOCATION 8
! AS A FLOATING-POINT OPERAND", second part: the STORE).
!
! Reference Manual printed p.96 (PDF 99), Store Rounded (SRD): "The
! rounding is performed by adding one to the fraction in the accumulator
! in bit position 60 ... The 48 low-order bits are discarded ... The
! sign of the accumulator, as changed by the sign modifiers, is placed
! in storage bit 60.  The accumulator flag bits are placed in storage
! bits 61-63.  The entire accumulator and its sign byte register remain
! unchanged throughout the operation unless used as the effective
! address."
!
! Here the effective address IS location 8.  The accumulator holds
! s*s, s = .6 as assembled (0009 9999 9999 9990), double length.  Its
! bits 60-63 are fraction bits 49-52 of s*s = 1110, so ROUNDING CARRIES
! INTO BIT 59: the stored fraction is B851E B851 EB7, the unrounded one
! ...EB6.  Worked by hand from p.96, "SRDN, $L" must leave in word 8
!   exponent -1, fraction rounded, sign 1 (N inverts plus), flags 000:
!   003B 851E B851 EB78
! and whatever p.96's "unless used as the effective address" does to
! $SB, bits 0-59 of word 8 must end ...EB7.
!
! THE MODEL, OBSERVED 2026-11-16 with words 8-10 dumped:
!   word 8   003B 851E B851 EB6E   bits 0-59 UNROUNDED, bits 60-63 the
!                                  accumulator's own fraction bits
!   word 10  0000 0000 0000 0000   $SB unchanged, still plus
! So the store did not happen at all, by either reading of p.96: it is
! not a sign byte routed to $SB instead of word 8.  (An earlier version
! of this deck used t*t, t = 1/3, whose rounding does not carry; it
! could not tell a lost store from a redirected sign byte.)
!
! Registered pinned at the model's WRONG words; flip both when fixed.
! SRT(N), $L (4.12, 4.13) DOES take effect in the model; this is SRD's.
!
! Found by C22-6578 Problem 4.9, printed p.43, "SRDN,$L", the last
! store of COSF (decks/problem_4_9_method1.strap).

START   DL(N), SIX
        D*(N), SIX
        SRDN, $L
HALT    BEW, $
SIX     DD(N), .6
        END, START
